WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.090
I typed just this to the agent,

2
00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:06.350
in Arabic: yes, send it.

3
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.380
Nobody had asked me anything.

4
00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:13.590
It made up a message, and sent it!

5
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.600
Wasn’t it trained to ask first?

6
00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.650
Today: permissions and

7
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.510
approval, checked in code.

8
00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.940
Every tool gets a permission level.

9
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.250
Read only: it may look things

10
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.350
up, like the weather.

11
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.860
Ask first: it waits for a person’s

12
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.020
yes, like a message to parents.

13
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:38.350
Allowed: it acts freely, for

14
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:39.510
low-risk jobs only.

15
00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.330
Darsi Tiny learned to ask before sending.

16
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.320
But learned behaviour can fail.

17
00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:49.570
Requests it should refuse, worded in

18
00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.810
new ways, still got a tool call

19
00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.490
twenty-eight percent of the time in

20
00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.410
English, and twelve percent in Arabic.

21
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.950
A promise to ask is not a lock.

22
00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.740
So the check belongs in

23
00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.380
code, outside the model.

24
00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:07.570
Before any action runs, the app asks: did

25
00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:10.250
the model ask this person about this exact

26
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.630
action, and did they say yes?

27
00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.200
If not, the call is blocked,

28
00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:16.560
however it’s worded.

29
00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.410
Here’s that check in code.

30
00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:23.790
It looks up the tool’s level, and a tool

31
00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.350
missing from the table counts as off.

32
00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:28.710
Allowed tools run.

33
00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:32.470
Ask-first tools run only after a yes.

34
00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:34.640
Everything else is blocked.

35
00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:38.170
Every action also goes in a log:

36
00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.590
what was asked, the exact call,

37
00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.490
who approved it and when.

38
00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.680
When a parent asks about a

39
00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:46.580
message, the log answers.

40
00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.680
Blocked calls go in too: they

41
00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:50.940
show where the agent slips.

42
00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:52.920
Quick check!

43
00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:57.270
Darsi Tiny learned to ask before sending.

44
00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:01.020
Why check the approval in code as well?

45
00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:04.510
Because learned behaviour can fail.

46
00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:07.770
New wordings slip past it, and on

47
00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.930
its own, an Arabic yes, send it made

48
00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.550
the model invent a message.

49
00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.910
The code check doesn’t guess: no yes

50
00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.590
to this exact action, no action.

51
00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.000
Now look at this code.

52
00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.560
When the model asks to send a

53
00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.960
message, the app just sends it.

54
00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.160
Nothing checks that a person

55
00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:31.320
said yes, so one slip becomes a

56
00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.080
message to every parent.

57
00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.820
In the app, send the message to Mrs

58
00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:40.420
Mensah: it asks first, so say no, then

59
00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:40.740
yes.

60
00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:43.010
Then switch the code check off,

61
00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.670
choose Allowed, and send the

62
00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:47.950
Arabic yes, send it on its own.

63
00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.740
Switch the check on and try again.

64
00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:52.710
Your turn.

65
00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:55.650
The agent wants to send the

66
00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.930
fees letter to all parents.

67
00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:00.800
What must happen first?

68
00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:04.660
A named person reads the exact

69
00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.420
message and says yes.

70
00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.320
Remember: every tool gets

71
00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:10.260
a permission level.

72
00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.770
Approval is checked in code,

73
00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:14.690
never only by the model.

74
00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.670
And every action is

75
00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:18.410
logged, blocked ones too.

76
00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:20.920
Try it in class tomorrow:

77
00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.640
run an approval drill.

78
00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:25.150
One pupil is the agent and

79
00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:26.430
hands over action cards.

80
00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.380
Another is the code check, with the

81
00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.780
permissions table, and blocks any

82
00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:33.920
action card without a signed yes.
